WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.712
Hello Stanford community, I'm Rob Siegel.

00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:05.810
&gt;&gt; I'm Lisa de Simone
&gt;&gt; My name is Ed Battista.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.454
&gt;&gt; I'm Britney Nicole's
&gt;&gt; Ashley Martin here.

00:00:08.454 --> 00:00:09.830
&gt;&gt; My name is Chun Woo Choi.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.780
&gt;&gt; I'm Kristen Wheeler.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.400
&gt;&gt; Hello, my name is Becky Lester.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.830
&gt;&gt; I'm Rod.
&gt;&gt; I'm I'm Zack Tormala.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.880
&gt;&gt; Hi folks, this is Sarah Singer.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.560
&gt;&gt; All the way here from my
house on Stanford campus.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.000
&gt;&gt; You can see it's incredibly quiet.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.100
We miss you all.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.960
&gt;&gt; Welcome to my home office, I mean,
my Stanford virtual teaching studio.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.100
Milo is going to be a part of the classes.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.375
&gt;&gt; This is my home assistant, Mr. Bongo.

00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:35.121
&gt;&gt; Josie, My trusted coated retriever,

00:00:35.121 --> 00:00:40.010
[LAUGH] is very happy to
have me around all day.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.070
&gt;&gt; We know these are really
uncertain times.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.110
&gt;&gt; I feel more connected to those
are who especially living in

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.280
different parts of the world.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.323
&gt;&gt; I know it's been difficult,
from the canceled plans,

00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:55.580
to the new anxieties, to the new
inability to be around people you love.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.592
&gt;&gt; At times like these, I try to focus on
things in life that I am grateful for.

00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:03.250
&gt;&gt; These are certainly going to
be trying times for all of us.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.730
We can all use a little
extra tending right now.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.228
&gt;&gt; One major silver lining for me in this
period has been that I'm getting to spend

00:01:09.228 --> 00:01:10.665
a lot more time with the family.

00:01:10.665 --> 00:01:13.966
&gt;&gt; What it makes me realize is that,
though Stanford is here,

00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:16.220
Stanford is actually where you all are.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.530
It's online at the moment.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.950
&gt;&gt; But then, I'm amazed at how
people have bonded together.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.730
&gt;&gt; It's been an opportunity
to take a step back.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.150
&gt;&gt; This quarter will be what we make it.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:29.540
&gt;&gt; It's really been pretty
miraculous the way people have

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.190
come together to make it all happen.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.445
&gt;&gt; To appreciate each other,

00:01:32.445 --> 00:01:35.780
because at the end of the day,
we are all in this together.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.300
And I have no doubt that we
are going to come out stronger and

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.815
more unified than ever before.

00:01:41.815 --> 00:01:46.110
&gt;&gt; In these times I think about how we
can make the best out of the situations.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.258
&gt;&gt; While we welcome you back,
we know these are not times that you would

00:01:49.258 --> 00:01:52.620
normally script for a spring
quarter of the 2020 academic year.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.740
&gt;&gt; So let's do our best.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.150
&gt;&gt; Thank you for
all you are and will be doing.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.660
I can't wait to see you
online this quarter.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.250
More importantly, I can't wait to
see you in person in the future.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:06.114
&gt;&gt; I certainly hope we see

00:02:06.114 --> 00:02:10.978
each other up close and

00:02:10.978 --> 00:02:14.563
in person soon.

00:02:14.563 --> 00:02:18.181
[MUSIC]

